1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:03,500
Graduate School staff signs in.

2
00:00:06,099 --> 00:00:13,900
The Monitoring Sheet, under Records: one row per student, one column per subject. Colours show completed, enrolled, or not yet taken.

3
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:23,699
Graduate School staff adds a student missing from the imported sheet. The window warns: manual entry, recorded with the staff member's name and time.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,599
Student ID, name and year of entry. The same required fields and duplicate checks as an import apply.

5
00:00:33,799 --> 00:00:37,199
The student is added, with a Student Portal login.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,299
The record panel lists all eighteen subjects, none taken yet, with units counted automatically.

7
00:00:45,700 --> 00:00:51,500
Graduate School staff adds a subject: status Completed, the term, and a remark.

8
00:00:54,899 --> 00:01:01,699
Both rows say Manual entry in the Source column, so manual data is never mistaken for imported data.

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
A remark is corrected with a simple edit.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,500
Removing a row needs a reason. The row returns to not taken and stays in the history.

11
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:29,700
The Change history tab shows every add, change and removal: old value, new value, who, when, source and reason. That is the audit trail.

12
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:38,099
Back on the grid, the new student carries a Manual tag, and hand-entered cells show an orange dot.

13
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:44,000
Now an imported student. Every row says Imported: official workbook values.

14
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:53,299
Changing an imported value requires a reason, recorded with the staff member's name. Grades are never entered here: AIMS is the official source.
